---
import WysDecor from '../../components/WysDecor.astro';
import WysShelf from '../../components/WysShelf.astro';
import WysPackage from '../../components/WysPackage.astro';
import WysStories from '../../components/WysStories.astro';
import WysFrame from '../../components/WysFrame.astro';
import WysHero from '../../components/WysHero.astro';
import WysWorksheet from '../../components/WysWorksheet.astro';
import WysKit from '../../components/WysKit.astro';
import WysFaq from '../../components/WysFaq.astro';
import {Image} from 'astro:assets';
import {packages} from '../../data/wys-packages.js';
import {WYS_ROOT} from '../../data/wys.js';
---
<WysFrame title="The While-You-Sleep Storefront™ | TDIE" description="Build Amazon affiliate content around your shopping ideas. Explore complete WYS examples with styling images, articles, Pinterest Pins and Instagram content." ogImage={packages[1].photos[1].src.src}>
 <WysHero><h1 class="wz-accessible-heading">The While-You-Sleep Storefront</h1><div class="wys-actions"><a class="wys-button" href="#full-example">View the examples ↓</a><a class="wys-text-link" href="#kit">See the kit ↓</a></div></WysHero>
 <WysShelf/><div class="wx-ticker"><span>3 STYLING IMAGES</span><span>3 PINTEREST GRAPHICS</span><span>3 INSTAGRAM SLIDES</span><span>ARTICLE + PRODUCTS + COPY</span></div>
 <section class="wys-wrap wys-section"><div class="wx-paper-strip"><div><p class="wys-label">One shopping idea. Content for several channels. A process to repeat.</p><h2>You found the products.<br/>Now comes everything else.</h2><p>The pictures. The article. The Pins. The carousel. The captions. The shopping links.</p></div><div><p>A Halloween coffee bar might start with five cute finds. Turning those finds into content means making a whole series of decisions before you have something to publish.</p><p>Then the next idea arrives, and you do it all again.</p><p>WYS gives that work a structure. Your product selection becomes the starting point for the visuals, writing and shopping destination, so you can build around one idea instead of inventing a separate idea for every channel.</p></div></div></section>
 <section class="wys-wrap wys-section" id="full-example"><div class="wx-centered"><p class="wys-label">Give one good shopping idea more places to go.</p><h2>Five Amazon finds.<br/>Everything built around them.</h2><p>Explore the images, read the full article and captions, and see the product records. Every piece belongs to the same look.</p></div><WysPackage example={packages[0]} number={1} tour/></section>
 <WysStories/>
 <section class="wx-process-band"><div class="wys-wrap wys-section"><div class="wx-centered"><p class="wys-label">From “I could make something with these”</p><h2>To a repeatable<br/>content routine.</h2></div><div class="wx-process">{[
 ['01 / Set up your business','Choose your niche, product categories, account path, channels, schedule and budget. Decide whether you want an AI persona and how much of the process you want to handle yourself.'],
 ['02 / Build your shopping idea','Choose the actual products. Record the right variants, details and affiliate links. Give the look a clear direction.'],
 ['03 / Create the visuals and content','Use the same selected pieces to guide your styling images, article, Pinterest content and Instagram content.'],
 ['04 / Connect it to a shopping destination','Prepare the destination supported by your account, then check the products, links and disclosures before publishing.'],
 ['05 / Publish, track and repeat','Follow the workflow for your next look. Keep the work you’ve completed and see what still needs attention, so the next step is easier to find.']
 ].map(([title,text])=><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{text}</p></div>)}</div></div></section>
 <section class="wys-wrap wys-section"><div class="wx-paper-strip"><div><h2>Your preferences belong in the setup, not in every new prompt.</h2><p>WYS is being built around reusable instructions for your business: what you feature, where your content goes, how often you post and what you’re comfortable spending.</p><p>That means a clearer starting point for the next outfit, room refresh, seasonal edit or shopping idea.</p></div><div><h2>Choose where AI helps and where you stay hands-on.</h2><p>Use a manual process, a mix of manual and automated steps, or supported automation after your setup has been tested.</p><p>Want to save credits? Handle more steps yourself.</p><p>Want help with recurring work? Use the connections your accounts support, within your chosen budget and approval settings.</p><p>An AI persona is optional. The workflow starts with your business choices.</p></div></div></section>
 <WysWorksheet/><div id="kit"><WysKit/></div>
 <section class="wys-wrap wys-section"><div class="wx-paths"><div><p class="wys-label">Made to fit your actual setup</p><h2>Build around<br/><em>your business.</em></h2><p>Choose the Amazon route, tools and level of involvement that fit your setup. Your budget, channels and preferences shape the process.</p></div><div class="wx-path-list"><div><b>Influencer route</b><p>Use eligible Amazon Idea Lists as the shopping destination for your content.</p></div><div><b>Associates-only route</b><p>Send readers to your own approved website page with the selected products and affiliate links.</p></div><div><b>Manual or mixed</b><p>Keep the steps you want to handle yourself, and add supported automation after testing your setup.</p></div><div><b>Optional persona & closet</b><p>Create with or without an AI persona. An optional Brand Closet path requires your own authorized membership.</p></div></div></div></section>
 <WysFaq/>
 <section class="wys-wrap wys-section"><div class="wx-last-call"><p class="wys-label">A little less to keep checking</p><h2>See what your next<br/>shopping idea could become.</h2><p>Open the complete examples and follow the products through the images, article, Pins and carousel. Want to keep up with TDIE while WYS is being finalized?</p><a class="wys-button" href={WYS_ROOT+'/waitlist'}>Get The Weekly Edit →</a></div></section>
</WysFrame>
